just tested in wizard mode, and you're right that Medusa is not like a
cockatrice.  You can handle her corpse without gloves, and wielding it
doesn't seem to stone creatures.  Eating her corpse is both stone-
inducing and poisonous, though.

If you're invisible and reflecting, her gaze will reflect, but she
won't seem to notice that her gaze was reflected and she won't die.
Even if you're invisible, you can apply a mirror against her to stone
her, though.

I got the 91% from this line of code in makemon.c:
return((boolean)(!!rn2(16 + (u.ualign.record < -15 ? -15 :
u.ualign.record)) && !!rn2(2 + abs(mal))));
u.ualign.record is probably high, so I basically ignored that.
I think mal should be the titan's alignment of 9, so I think we're
talking about 10 chances in 11 that a titan is peaceful.  If your
alignment record is only 20, then I think the total percentage would
be 88%.

I do think that's a major advantage to playing lawful.  I would think
that a neutral or chaotic character could easily get stuck with no way
to get across the Medusa Level without first finding some nice
equipment (like a wand of death or ring of poly control).  not being
able to wish for the Eye of the Aethiopica (or Eyes of the Overworld)
is a bummer, though.

I generally wouldn't worry too much about the caitiff message.  If you
keep killing things the -1 penalty to alignment shouldn't be
important.
Some monsters are generated asleep.  Some rooms of monsters have
monsters generated asleep.  If you have stealth, then you might be
attacking them while they're still asleep.

Have you tried jumping while wearing the jungle boots?  You might be
able to jump farther with them than the normal knight's jump, which
can be useful in certain situations.  especially while on a fast mount
where you don't care as much about speed boots.


